# Peer resolution has to stay off for this project.
#
# react-native-worklets declares `@react-native/metro-config` as a hard peer,
# which drags upstream metro in alongside the metro Expo vendors as
# @expo/metro. npm then treats them as conflicting, hoists upstream metro to
# the top level, and pushes Expo's own toolchain (babel-preset-expo, @expo/cli,
# @expo/metro-config) into node_modules/expo/node_modules — at which point
# @babel/core can no longer resolve babel-preset-expo and every bundle fails
# with "Cannot find module 'babel-preset-expo'".
#
# This was previously set only in Josh's user-level ~/.npmrc, so local installs
# skipped peers and CI (which has no such setting) did not — `npm ci` failed
# with EUSAGE on peers the lockfile never recorded. Pinning it here is what
# makes the two agree.
legacy-peer-deps=true
